bw.lore.1=§l1785§r\n\nIn the village of Blair, Maryland, several children accuse a woman, Elly Kedward, of luring them into her home to draw their blood.\n\nShe is declared a witch. In the dead of winter she is tied to a cart and left in the woods. Everyone presumes her dead.
bw.lore.2=§l1786§r\n\nThe next winter, all of Elly Kedward's accusers vanish, along with half of the village's children.\n\nThe rest flee and swear never to speak her name again. Blair is abandoned.
bw.lore.3=§l1824§r\n\nA new town is founded on the ruins of Blair: Burkittsville.\n\nNobody talks about what happened before.
bw.lore.4=§l1825§r\n\nA girl drowns in a shallow creek. Several witnesses swear they saw a pale hand rise from the water and pull her under.\n\nFor days the creek is choked with bundles of oily sticks.
bw.lore.5=§l1886§r\n\nA girl, Robin Weaver, goes missing in the woods. A search party goes out.\n\nThe girl comes home on her own. The search party does not. They are found later at Coffin Rock, tied to one another. No one can explain what happened to them.
bw.lore.6=§l1940 - 1941§r\n\nA hermit named Rustin Parr takes seven children to his house in the woods.\n\nWhen he turns himself in, he says he made one child stand facing the corner while he hurt the other. He says an old woman, a spirit of the woods, told him what to do.
bw.lore.7=§lOctober 1994§r\n\nThree film students, Heather, Josh and Mike, hike into the Black Hills Forest to make a documentary about the legend.\n\nThey never come back.
bw.lore.8=§l1995§r\n\nA year later, their footage is found in the woods.\n\n§oNow it's your turn to film.
